Read the first expected_output carefully: the inline script body keeps its indentation and internal newlines byte-for-byte while the surrounding head collapses to one line — and the opening script tags re-emit their attributes alphabetized (charset, src, type / charset, language, type) even though they're protected regions. The blank line inside the textarea in case two survives untouched. These behaviors are contract, not accident.
